                "caption": "Figure 1:Open Vision Banana overview.A source imagexxand a task instructionpqp_{q}condition a frozen generative backbone (Qwen-Image-2.1 in all experiments; the backbone is a configuration choice) that carries one newly initialized rank-64 LoRA adapterδ\\deltashared by all tasks. The source enters as visual tokens and reference latents, the instruction as the text condition, and the target latent is generated from noise in 50 flow steps. The generated RGB imager^q\\hat{r}_{q}is converted by a parameter-free decoderDqD_{q}into a structured predictiony^q\\hat{y}_{q}: metric depth, a class-ID map, instance masks, or a binary mask. Bottom: a task contract𝒞q=(Eq,pq,Dq,Sq)\\mathcal{C}_{q}=(E_{q},p_{q},D_{q};S_{q})ties encoder, instruction, and decoder to one specification and is validated before training. The scene is a rendered illustration; its RGB tiles are produced by the contract encoders from exact annotations and are not model predictions.",
